Many of the thermal features at Whakarewarewa have been adversely affected by Rotorua residents taking advantage of the underlying geothermal fluids of the city by drawing shallow wells (20–200 m [66–656 ft] deep) to extract hot water for both domestic and commercial heating. A bore closure programme in 1987–1988 resulted in 106 wells within 1.5 km (0.93 mi) of Pōhutu Geyser being cemented...","coordinates":[{"lat":-38.16222222,"lon":176.25638889,"primary":true,"globe":"earth"}],"pageimage":"WhakarewarewaAerial.jpg","pageprops":{"page_image_free":"WhakarewarewaAerial.jpg","wikibase-shortdesc":"Suburb of Rotorua, New Zealand","wikibase_item":"Q1134836"}}]}}
